# --- registry -------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by setup/lib/models.sh; passed to llama-server as environment and
# ignored there. MODEL_SWA=yes means the profile MUST carry --swa-full —
# without it every Claude Code turn re-processes the whole prompt.
MODEL_TITLE=Batch classification · Gemma 4 26B · 5 prompt variants, 8k window
MODEL_SWA=yes
# MODEL_SOURCE — where this model comes from, so the profile can fetch it.
# `<repo> <pattern>…`: every pattern is a substring of a path in that repo and
# every matching .gguf is fetched, so a sharded quant comes down whole and an
# mmproj rides along. Read by setup/get-model.sh, which is this stack's
# equivalent of `ollama pull` — except that the list it offers is MEASURED on
# this hardware (bash setup/lib/models.sh table) rather than a generic catalog.
# Verified 26.08. by matching the exact filename in the repo, not by guessing.
MODEL_SOURCE=google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-qat-q4_0-gguf gemma-4-26B_q4_0-it
# MODEL_KV_KIB_PER_TOKEN — measured, and it is the SAME WEIGHTS as gemma26,
# which is why the number may be carried over here and nowhere else. Read by
# setup/lib/budget.py.
MODEL_KV_KIB_PER_TOKEN=10.4
MODEL_KV_SOURCE=gemma26's measurement, same model file: 1.3 GiB at -c 131072, i.e. 10.4 KiB per token.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Batch classification (runbook section 20) · a different load profile than interactive
# -np = number of prompt variants, -c deliberately small, no speculative decoding
# -cram WAS 16384, and 16 GiB of RAM prompt cache for an 8,192-token window
# buys 197 FULL WINDOWS. Measured 27.08. by `python3 setup/lib/budget.py
# --cache`, the first time anything asked what the flag buys rather than
# whether it fits:
#
#     KV per window   8,192 x 10.4 KiB   =  0.08 GiB
#     -cram 16384                        = 16.0 GiB  -> 197 windows
#     -cram 1024                         =  1.0 GiB  ->  12 windows
#
# 12 is still generous for five prompt variants. 197 is not headroom, it is a
# number that was copied from a profile with a 25x larger window and never
# read. Frees 15 GiB on any machine that runs this alongside something else.
# --- reasoning modes ------------------------------------------------------
#
# The rule and the vocabulary: setup/claude/modes.py. The two lines below are
# GENERATED — `python3 bench/suites/effort-vocabulary.py --profile batch` —
# and everything model-specific about them is the measurement that follows.
#
# MEASURED 28.08.2026. This template (sha ae53464bf3be, shared by gemma26,
# gemma31 and batch) reads `enable_thinking` and IGNORES `reasoning_effort`
# completely: all six levels render byte-identically. So every level word means
# the same thing here — thinking on — and they share one prefix id rather than
# five.
#
# No `none` mode: measured, this template's DEFAULT is not to think (unset and
# enable_thinking=false both render eb138503), so `none` would be the same
# prompt under a second cache key. laguna measures the opposite way round,
# which is why this is per model and not assumed.
#
# TEMPLATE_LEVELS says `no-levels`, which is a measurement and not an empty
# field: an absent line and an empty one read back identically, so silence
# would have switched the load-time check off instead of narrowing it.
MODES=low:on  medium:on  high:on  xhigh:on  max:on
TEMPLATE_LEVELS=no-levels
#
LLAMA_ARGS=--alias batch -m @MODELS@/gemma-4-26B_q4_0-it.gguf \
  -ngl 999 -fa on -np 5 --kv-unified -c 8192 -b 4096 -ub 2048 \
  -ctk q8_0 -ctv q8_0 -cram 1024 -ctxcp 64 -cms 4096 \
  --slot-save-path /var/cache/llama --no-slots \
  --jinja --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8083

# Backend for this profile. Measured 24.08. (docs/MODELS.md): the choice
# is MODEL-dependent — Vulkan wins for models without speculation, ROCm wins
# 2x once MTP/ngram speculation is on. Inert until llama-user@.service is
# switched to: ExecStart=/bin/sh -c 'exec "$HOME/$LLAMA_BIN" $LLAMA_ARGS' (one sudo install).
LLAMA_BIN=llama.cpp/build-vulkan/bin/llama-server
